WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:06.523
A three hundred year old oak still makes new shoots and wood.

2
00:00:07.403 --> 00:00:11.663
It keeps regions of dividing cells, called meristems, for as long as it lives.

3
00:00:12.543 --> 00:00:14.063
These supply new cells and organs.

4
00:00:15.023 --> 00:00:17.723
That is how many plants keep building their bodies for years.

5
00:00:18.763 --> 00:00:21.383
Apical meristems at root and shoot tips add length.

6
00:00:21.383 --> 00:00:23.803
Lateral meristems add girth.

7
00:00:24.717 --> 00:00:25.957
Follow a root tip.

8
00:00:26.837 --> 00:00:30.297
Under its protective cap, small cells divide in the zone of division.

9
00:00:31.257 --> 00:00:36.057
In the zone of elongation, cells stop dividing and lengthen as water fills their

10
00:00:36.057 --> 00:00:41.437
vacuoles. In the zone of maturation, they become their final types, and root hairs

11
00:00:41.437 --> 00:00:42.437
appear.

12
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.340
Division supplies cells.

13
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:46.680
Elongation sets their length.

14
00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:52.280
At steady state, with every cell file alike, root growth rate equals new cells per

15
00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.580
file per hour times final cell length.

16
00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:56.560
Take illustrative numbers.

17
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.680
1 cell per hour times 300 µm gives 300 µm per hour.

18
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.700
These numbers are not from a measured species.

19
00:01:06.883 --> 00:01:08.223
Now look at the oak trunk.

20
00:01:09.103 --> 00:01:14.323
Its vascular cambium adds secondary xylem inward and secondary phloem outward.

21
00:01:15.303 --> 00:01:16.603
Secondary xylem is wood.

22
00:01:17.463 --> 00:01:21.923
A different meristem, the cork cambium, makes cork outward and living phelloderm

23
00:01:21.923 --> 00:01:27.003
inward. Together with the cork cambium, these form the periderm, replacing the

24
00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:30.963
epidermis. Bark is everything outside the vascular cambium.

25
00:01:31.763 --> 00:01:33.123
It includes living phloem.

26
00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:35.767
These new cells build tissues.

27
00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:40.687
Xylem and phloem are complex tissues, each made of several cell types.

28
00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:42.647
They connect plant organs.

29
00:01:43.807 --> 00:01:44.807
Xylem carries water.

30
00:01:45.807 --> 00:01:47.887
Phloem carries sugars and amino acids.

31
00:01:48.827 --> 00:01:51.407
Together they belong to the vascular tissue system.

32
00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.510
In a leaf, veins carry both tissues.

33
00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:57.590
Chloroplasts in the mesophyll capture light.

34
00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:02.590
Air spaces connect to stomata, pores opened and closed by guard cells.

35
00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:07.170
An open stoma lets carbon dioxide in and water vapour out.

36
00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.010
The leaf gains carbon at a cost in water.
